  InterfaceDecl
    LineComment "// Interface inheritance (supertraits): an interface may list one or more parent"
    Newline "\n"
    LineComment "// interfaces after a colon, and a child inherits their whole contract — every"
    Newline "\n"
    LineComment "// required and provided member. Inheritance carries requirements only; there is"
    Newline "\n"
    LineComment "// no state and no implementation hierarchy (a child cannot exist), so a child is"
    Newline "\n"
    LineComment "// simply the union of its own members and its ancestors'. A type that opts into"
    Newline "\n"
    LineComment "// the child opts into every ancestor too: writing `impl <child>` materializes"
    Newline "\n"
    LineComment "// the ancestors onto the type, so a bound or switch reading the parent contract"
    Newline "\n"
    LineComment "// is satisfied through the child alone."
    Newline "\n"
    Newline "\n"
    DocComment "/// A behaviour layered on a parent: a printable value is comparable, so it"
    Newline "\n"
    DocComment "/// carries eql/neq (from comparable) on top of its own show."
    Newline "\n"
